{"tool_name":"sdm","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"sdm","identifiers":["biotools:sdm","doi:10.1093/nar/gkr363"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"sdm - simple demultiplex tool for FASTQ demultiplexing and dereplication","home_url":"https://github.com/hildebra/sdm/","keywords":["Amino Acid Substitution","Disease","Humans","Internet","Mutation","Protein Conformation","Protein Stability","Proteins","Thermodynamics","Protein folding, stability and design","Genetic variation","Small molecules","Gene and protein families","Structure prediction"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"sdm","home":"http://www-cryst.bioc.cam.ac.uk/~sdm/sdm.php","summary":"Site Directed Mutator (SDM) is a web server for predicting effects of mutations on protein stability and function. Users input a wild type structure and the position and amino acid type of the mutation. An environment specific amino acid substitution frequency for homologous protein families is used to calculate a stability score.","addition_date":"2017-02-14T09:35:46Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:54Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:sdm","credit":[{"email":"apandura@mrc-lmb.cam.ac.uk","name":"ARUN PRASAD PANDURANGAN","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://131.111.43.103/help"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Protein function prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_1777"},{"term":"Protein model validation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0321"},{"term":"Protein modelling (mutation)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0331"},{"term":"Protein secondary structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0267"},{"term":"Protein structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0474"}]}],"name":"SDM","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"The sheer volume of non-synonymous single nucleotide polymorphisms that have been generated in recent years from projects such as the Human Genome Project, the HapMap Project and Genome-Wide Association Studies means that it is not possible to characterize all mutations experimentally on the gene products, i.e. elucidate the effects of mutations on protein structure and function. However, automatic methods that can predict the effects of mutations will allow a reduced set of mutations to be studied. Site Directed Mutator (SDM) is a statistical potential energy function that uses environment-specific amino-acid substitution frequencies within homologous protein families to calculate a stability score, which is analogous to the free energy difference between the wild-type and mutant protein. Here, we present a web server for SDM (http://www-cryst.bioc.cam.ac.uk/\u223csdm/sdm.php), which has obtained more than 10000 submissions since being online in April 2008. To run SDM, users must upload a wild-type structure and the position and amino acid type of the mutation. The results returned include information about the local structural environment of the wild-type and mutant residues, a stability score prediction and prediction of disease association. Additionally, the wild-type and mutant structures are displayed in a Jmol applet with the relevant residues highlighted. \u00a9 2011 The Author(s).","authors":[{"name":"Blundell T.L."},{"name":"Preissner R."},{"name":"Worth C.L."}],"citationCount":314,"date":"2011-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"SDM - A server for predicting effects of mutations on protein stability and malfunction"},"pmid":"21593128"}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene and protein families","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0623"},{"term":"Genetic variation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0199"},{"term":"Protein folding, stability and design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0130"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"},{"term":"Structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0082"}],"validated":1},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:sdm/web/www-cryst.bioc.cam.ac.uk","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true,"help":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":271,"citations":[{"count":2,"year":"-1"},{"count":8,"year":"2012"},{"count":12,"year":"2026"},{"count":13,"year":"2014"},{"count":13,"year":"2018"},{"count":16,"year":"2020"},{"count":16,"year":"2021"},{"count":17,"year":"2013"},{"count":17,"year":"2017"},{"count":19,"year":"2015"},{"count":19,"year":"2025"},{"count":21,"year":"2016"},{"count":23,"year":"2022"},{"count":24,"year":"2019"},{"count":24,"year":"2024"},{"count":27,"year":"2023"}],"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkr363","pmcid":"PMC3125769","pmid":"21593128","ref_count":71,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1971"},{"count":1,"year":"1990"},{"count":1,"year":"1991"},{"count":1,"year":"1995"},{"count":2,"year":"1987"},{"count":2,"year":"1992"},{"count":2,"year":"1993"},{"count":2,"year":"1997"},{"count":2,"year":"2000"},{"count":2,"year":"2001"},{"count":2,"year":"2002"},{"count":2,"year":"2003"},{"count":3,"year":"1998"},{"count":4,"year":"2008"},{"count":6,"year":"2005"},{"count":6,"year":"2006"},{"count":7,"year":"2004"},{"count":7,"year":"2010"},{"count":9,"year":"2007"},{"count":9,"year":"2009"}],"title":"SDM--a server for predicting effects of mutations on protein stability and malfunction.","year":2011}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":408,"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"email":true}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/bioconda:sdm:2.05/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@